#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit compilation transforms a high-level quantum algorithm into a physical circuit that respects the constraints of the target hardware. Effective compilation can significantly reduce circuit depth and gate count, both of which directly impact the quality of results on near-term quantum devices.\n"
msgstr "Kompilasi litar kuantum mengubah algoritma kuantum peringkat tinggi kepada litar fizikal yang mematuhi kekangan perkakasan sasaran. Kompilasi yang berkesan boleh mengurangkan kedalaman litar dan bilangan gate dengan ketara, yang secara langsung mempengaruhi kualiti keputusan pada peranti kuantum jangka pendek.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial benchmarks three compilation methods on Hamiltonian simulation circuits built with `PauliEvolutionGate`. These circuits model pairwise qubit interactions (such as $ZZ$, $XX$, and $YY$ terms) and are common in quantum chemistry, condensed matter physics, and materials science.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menanda aras tiga kaedah kompilasi pada litar simulasi Hamiltonian yang dibina dengan `PauliEvolutionGate`. Litar ini memodelkan interaksi berpasangan qubit (seperti sebutan $ZZ$, $XX$, dan $YY$) dan lazim digunakan dalam kimia kuantum, fizik jirim pekat, dan sains bahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The benchmark circuits come from the [Hamlib](https://github.com/SRI-International/QC-App-Oriented-Benchmarks/tree/master/qedcbench/hamlib#hamlib-simulation---benchmark-program) collection, accessed through the [Benchpress](https://github.com/Qiskit/benchpress) repository. Hamlib provides a standardized set of representative Hamiltonians, making it possible to compare compilation strategies on realistic simulation workloads.\n"
msgstr "Litar penanda aras diambil daripada koleksi [Hamlib](https://github.com/SRI-International/QC-App-Oriented-Benchmarks/tree/master/qedcbench/hamlib#hamlib-simulation---benchmark-program), yang diakses melalui repositori [Benchpress](https://github.com/Qiskit/benchpress). Hamlib menyediakan set Hamiltonian perwakilan yang distandardkan, memungkinkan perbandingan strategi kompilasi pada beban kerja simulasi yang realistik.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compilation methods overview {#compilation-methods-overview}"
msgstr "Gambaran keseluruhan kaedah kompilasi {#compilation-methods-overview}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit transpiler with SABRE {#qiskit-transpiler-with-sabre}"
msgstr "Qiskit transpiler dengan SABRE {#qiskit-transpiler-with-sabre}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit transpiler uses the SABRE (SWAP-based BidiREctional heuristic search) algorithm to optimize circuit layout and routing. SABRE focuses on minimizing SWAP gates and their impact on circuit depth while respecting hardware connectivity constraints. It is a general-purpose method that provides a good balance between performance and compilation time. For more details, see [\\[1\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08368). The advantages and parameter exploration of SABRE are covered in-depth in a separate [tutorial](/tutorials/transpilation-optimizations-with-sabre).\n"
msgstr "Qiskit transpiler menggunakan algoritma SABRE (SWAP-based BidiREctional heuristic search) untuk mengoptimumkan susunan dan penghalaan litar. SABRE menumpukan pada meminimumkan gate SWAP dan kesannya terhadap kedalaman litar sambil mematuhi kekangan kesambungan perkakasan. Ini adalah kaedah tujuan umum yang memberikan keseimbangan yang baik antara prestasi dan masa kompilasi. Untuk maklumat lanjut, lihat [\\[1\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08368). Kelebihan dan penerokaan parameter SABRE dibincangkan secara mendalam dalam [tutorial berasingan](/tutorials/transpilation-optimizations-with-sabre).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "AI-powered transpiler {#ai-powered-transpiler}"
msgstr "Transpiler berkuasa AI {#ai-powered-transpiler}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The AI-powered transpiler uses machine learning to predict optimal transpilation strategies by analyzing patterns in circuit structure and hardware constraints. It can also apply the `AIPauliNetworkSynthesis` pass, which targets Pauli network circuits using a reinforcement learning-based synthesis approach. For more information, see [\\[2\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.13196) and [\\[3\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14448).\n"
msgstr "Transpiler berkuasa AI menggunakan pembelajaran mesin untuk meramalkan strategi transpilasi optimum dengan menganalisis corak dalam struktur litar dan kekangan perkakasan. Ia juga boleh menggunakan laluan `AIPauliNetworkSynthesis`, yang mensasar litar rangkaian Pauli menggunakan pendekatan sintesis berasaskan pembelajaran pengukuhan. Untuk maklumat lanjut, lihat [\\[2\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.13196) dan [\\[3\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14448).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rustiq plugin {#rustiq-plugin}"
msgstr "Plugin Rustiq {#rustiq-plugin}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Rustiq plugin provides advanced synthesis techniques specifically for `PauliEvolutionGate` operations, which represent Pauli rotations commonly used in Trotterized dynamics. It is designed to produce low-depth circuit decompositions for Hamiltonian simulation workloads. For more details, see [\\[4\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.03280).\n"
msgstr "Plugin Rustiq menyediakan teknik sintesis lanjutan khusus untuk operasi `PauliEvolutionGate`, yang mewakili putaran Pauli yang biasa digunakan dalam dinamik Trotterisasi. Ia direka untuk menghasilkan penguraian litar berkedalaman rendah bagi beban kerja simulasi Hamiltonian. Untuk maklumat lanjut, lihat [\\[4\\]](https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.03280).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key metrics {#key-metrics}"
msgstr "Metrik utama {#key-metrics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We compare the three methods on the following metrics:\n"
"- **Two-qubit depth**: The depth of the circuit counting only two-qubit gates. This is often the bottleneck for fidelity on real hardware.\n"
"- **Circuit size (total gate count)**: The total number of gates in the transpiled circuit.\n"
"- **Runtime**: The wall-clock time for transpilation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami membandingkan ketiga-tiga kaedah berdasarkan metrik berikut:\n"
"- **Kedalaman dua-Qubit**: Kedalaman litar yang mengira hanya gate dua-Qubit. Ini sering menjadi kesesakan bagi ketepatan pada perkakasan sebenar.\n"
"- **Saiz litar (jumlah bilangan gate)**: Jumlah bilangan gate dalam litar yang ditranspilasi.\n"
"- **Masa jalan**: Masa jam dinding untuk transpilasi.\n"

