#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connect to a backend {#connect-to-a-backend}"
msgstr "Sambung ke backend {#connect-to-a-backend}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select a backend that will be used for both the small-scale and large-scale examples. The backend determines the coupling map and basis gates that the transpiler targets.\n"
msgstr "Pilih backend yang akan digunakan untuk kedua-dua contoh kecil dan besar. Backend menentukan peta gandingan dan gate asas yang disasarkan oleh transpiler.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define pass managers {#define-pass-managers}"
msgstr "Tentukan pengurus laluan {#define-pass-managers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the three compilation methods.\n"
msgstr "Sediakan ketiga-tiga kaedah kompilasi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define helper functions {#define-helper-functions}"
msgstr "Tentukan fungsi pembantu {#define-helper-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following function transpiles a list of circuits using a given pass manager, and records the key metrics (two-qubit depth, circuit size, and runtime) for each circuit.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi berikut mentranspilasi senarai litar menggunakan pengurus laluan yang diberikan, dan merekod metrik utama (kedalaman dua-Qubit, saiz litar, dan masa jalan) untuk setiap litar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load Hamiltonian circuits from Hamlib {#load-hamiltonian-circuits-from-hamlib}"
msgstr "Muatkan litar Hamiltonian daripada Hamlib {#load-hamiltonian-circuits-from-hamlib}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We load a representative set of Hamiltonians from the Benchpress repository and construct `PauliEvolutionGate` circuits. Circuits that exceed the backend's qubit count are removed, along with circuits whose decomposed size exceeds 1,500 gates (to keep transpilation times reasonable).\n"
msgstr "Kami memuatkan set Hamiltonian perwakilan daripada repositori Benchpress dan membina litar `PauliEvolutionGate`. Litar yang melebihi bilangan Qubit backend dibuang, bersama litar yang saiz terurai melebihi 1,500 gate (untuk memastikan masa transpilasi yang munasabah).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split circuits into small-scale (fewer than 20 qubits) and large-scale (20 or more qubits) groups.\n"
msgstr "Pisahkan litar kepada kumpulan berskala kecil (kurang daripada 20 Qubit) dan berskala besar (20 atau lebih Qubit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preview one of the small-scale Hamiltonian circuits before transpilation.\n"
msgstr "Pratonton salah satu litar Hamiltonian berskala kecil sebelum transpilasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/b4c5d6e7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/b4c5d6e7-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale example {#small-scale-example}"
msgstr "Contoh berskala kecil {#small-scale-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this section, we benchmark the three compilation methods on Hamiltonian circuits with fewer than 20 qubits. These circuits transpile quickly and provide a clear view of how each method handles circuits of moderate complexity.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian ini, kami menanda aras ketiga-tiga kaedah kompilasi pada litar Hamiltonian dengan kurang daripada 20 Qubit. Litar ini ditranspilasi dengan cepat dan memberikan gambaran jelas tentang bagaimana setiap kaedah mengendalikan litar dengan kerumitan sederhana.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasikal kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each Hamiltonian is encoded as a `PauliEvolutionGate` circuit. The circuits were already constructed in the setup section from the Hamlib benchmark data.\n"
msgstr "Setiap Hamiltonian dikodkan sebagai litar `PauliEvolutionGate`. Litar-litar ini telah dibina dalam bahagian persediaan daripada data penanda aras Hamlib.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We transpile all small-scale circuits using each of the three pass managers, then collect the metrics.\n"
msgstr "Kami mentranspilasi semua litar berskala kecil menggunakan setiap daripada tiga pengurus laluan, kemudian mengumpul metrik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The table below summarizes the average and standard deviation of each metric across all small-scale circuits, along with the percent improvement relative to SABRE. Because circuit sizes vary widely, the standard deviation provides important context for interpreting the averages.\n"
msgstr "Jadual di bawah merumuskan purata dan sisihan piawai setiap metrik merentasi semua litar berskala kecil, bersama peratusan penambahbaikan berbanding SABRE. Oleh kerana saiz litar berbeza-beza dengan ketara, sisihan piawai memberikan konteks penting untuk mentafsir purata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The per-circuit table shows how each method compares on individual circuits. The best value for each metric is marked with an asterisk. Notice that for the simplest circuits, all three methods often converge to the same result.\n"
msgstr "Jadual per-litar menunjukkan bagaimana setiap kaedah dibandingkan pada litar individu. Nilai terbaik untuk setiap metrik ditandai dengan asterisk. Perhatikan bahawa untuk litar yang paling mudah, ketiga-tiga kaedah sering menumpu kepada hasil yang sama.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize results {#visualize-results}"
msgstr "Visualisasi keputusan {#visualize-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plots below compare the three methods across each metric on a per-circuit basis. Circuits are sorted by qubit count and labeled by index on the x-axis, since multiple circuits can share the same number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "Plot di bawah membandingkan ketiga-tiga kaedah merentasi setiap metrik berdasarkan per-litar. Litar disusun mengikut bilangan Qubit dan dilabelkan mengikut indeks pada paksi-x, kerana beberapa litar boleh mempunyai bilangan Qubit yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/d5e6f7a8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/d5e6f7a8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/pct_improvement_small-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/pct_improvement_small-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this scale, all three pass managers perform well, and their average results are close to each other. This is largely because small circuits leave limited room for further optimization, so the methods tend to converge on similar solutions.\n"
msgstr "Pada skala ini, ketiga-tiga pengurus laluan berprestasi baik, dan purata keputusan mereka hampir sama. Ini sebahagian besarnya kerana litar kecil meninggalkan ruang terhad untuk pengoptimuman lanjut, jadi kaedah-kaedah cenderung menumpu kepada penyelesaian yang serupa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, Rustiq produces the most variable results, with the largest outliers in both two-qubit depth and gate count. While this variability means it sometimes falls behind, it also means Rustiq occasionally finds better solutions than the other two methods. The AI transpiler is more stable in its results relative to SABRE and Rustiq, tracking closely on most circuits without many outliers.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini, Rustiq menghasilkan keputusan yang paling pelbagai, dengan pencilan terbesar dalam kedalaman dua-Qubit dan bilangan gate. Walaupun kepelbagaian ini bermakna ia kadangkala ketinggalan, ia juga bermakna Rustiq kadangkala menemui penyelesaian yang lebih baik daripada dua kaedah lain. Transpiler AI lebih stabil dalam keputusannya berbanding SABRE dan Rustiq, mengikuti rapat pada kebanyakan litar tanpa banyak pencilan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For runtime, SABRE and Rustiq are both fast, while the AI-powered transpiler is noticeably slower on certain circuits.\n"
msgstr "Untuk masa jalan, SABRE dan Rustiq kedua-duanya pantas, manakala transpiler berkuasa AI jauh lebih perlahan pada litar tertentu.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best-performing method by metric {#best-performing-method-by-metric}"
msgstr "Kaedah berprestasi terbaik mengikut metrik {#best-performing-method-by-metric}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The chart below shows how often each method achieved the best (lowest) value for each metric. Ties are possible: for simpler circuits, multiple methods can reach the same optimal two-qubit depth or gate count. When a tie occurs, all tied methods receive credit, so the percentages for a given metric may sum to more than 100%.\n"
msgstr "Carta di bawah menunjukkan seberapa kerap setiap kaedah mencapai nilai terbaik (terendah) untuk setiap metrik. Seri adalah mungkin: untuk litar yang lebih mudah, beberapa kaedah boleh mencapai kedalaman dua-Qubit atau bilangan gate optimum yang sama. Apabila seri berlaku, semua kaedah yang seri menerima kredit, jadi peratusan untuk metrik tertentu mungkin berjumlah lebih daripada 100%.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/a6b7c8d9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/a6b7c8d9-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, the three methods perform very similarly on the small-scale circuits. On two-qubit depth and gate count, the share of circuits where each method is best is close (roughly 35–55%), and many circuits end in ties because the simplest circuits often have a single optimal solution that multiple methods find. The clearest difference is runtime: SABRE and Rustiq are each fastest on about half the circuits, while the AI-powered transpiler is rarely the quickest. Considering all three metrics together, Rustiq has a slight overall edge &nbsp; it is the most frequent winner on two-qubit depth and stays competitive on gate count and runtime.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh ini, ketiga-tiga kaedah berprestasi sangat serupa pada litar berskala kecil. Pada kedalaman dua-Qubit dan bilangan gate, bahagian litar di mana setiap kaedah adalah terbaik hampir sama (lebih kurang 35–55%), dan banyak litar berakhir dengan seri kerana litar yang paling mudah sering mempunyai satu penyelesaian optimum yang ditemui oleh beberapa kaedah. Perbezaan yang paling jelas adalah masa jalan: SABRE dan Rustiq masing-masing adalah yang terpantas pada lebih kurang separuh litar, manakala transpiler berkuasa AI jarang menjadi yang tercepat. Mempertimbangkan ketiga-tiga metrik bersama, Rustiq mempunyai kelebihan keseluruhan yang sedikit &nbsp; ia adalah pemenang paling kerap pada kedalaman dua-Qubit dan kekal berdaya saing pada bilangan gate dan masa jalan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To evaluate how transpilation quality affects execution under noise, we use a **mirror circuit** technique. For each transpiled circuit $U$, we append its inverse $U^\\dagger$ so the combined circuit $U^\\dagger U$ is theoretically the identity. Starting from the $|0\\rangle$ state, a perfect (noiseless) execution would return the all-zeros bitstring with probability 1.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menilai bagaimana kualiti transpilasi mempengaruhi pelaksanaan di bawah hingar, kami menggunakan teknik **litar cermin**. Untuk setiap litar yang ditranspilasi $U$, kami menambahkan inversnya $U^\\dagger$ supaya litar gabungan $U^\\dagger U$ adalah identiti secara teori. Bermula dari keadaan $|0\\rangle$, pelaksanaan sempurna (tanpa hingar) akan mengembalikan bitstring semua-sifar dengan kebarangkalian 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, gate errors accumulate throughout the circuit, so the probability of recovering $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ drops. A compilation method that produces a shallower circuit with fewer gates will accumulate less noise.\n"
msgstr "Dalam praktik, ralat gate terkumpul sepanjang litar, jadi kebarangkalian memulihkan $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ menurun. Kaedah kompilasi yang menghasilkan litar yang lebih cetek dengan gate yang lebih sedikit akan mengumpul lebih sedikit hingar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mirror circuit approach is appealingly simple and scales to any circuit size, since the expected output is always $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ and no classical simulation of the ideal state is required. However, note the following caveats: the mirror circuit is a proxy for the actual circuit (not the circuit itself), it doubles the gate count (which exaggerates the effect of noise), and it can underestimate certain errors when noise cancels symmetrically across the mirror boundary.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan litar cermin ini mudah dan berskala kepada mana-mana saiz litar, kerana output yang dijangka sentiasa $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ dan tiada simulasi klasikal keadaan ideal diperlukan. Walau bagaimanapun, perhatikan kaveat berikut: litar cermin adalah proksi untuk litar sebenar (bukan litar itu sendiri), ia menggandakan bilangan gate (yang membesar-besarkan kesan hingar), dan ia boleh meremehkan ralat tertentu apabila hingar membatal secara simetri merentasi sempadan cermin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We pick circuit index 6 from the small-scale set and run the mirror circuits on an Aer simulator with a simple depolarizing noise model.\n"
msgstr "Kami memilih litar indeks 6 daripada set berskala kecil dan menjalankan litar cermin pada simulator Aer dengan model hingar depolarisasi mudah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the mirror circuits (append $U^\\dagger$), remap to contiguous qubit indices so the simulator only handles the active qubits, and run on a noisy Aer simulator.\n"
msgstr "Bina litar cermin (tambahkan $U^\\dagger$), petakan semula kepada indeks Qubit berterusan supaya simulator hanya mengendalikan Qubit aktif, dan jalankan pada simulator Aer yang berising.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/small_step4_plot-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/compilation-methods-for-hamiltonian-simulation-circuits/extracted-outputs/small_step4_plot-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observations {#observations}"
msgstr "Pemerhatian {#observations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method with the lowest two-qubit depth and fewest gates achieves the highest fidelity, consistent with the expectation that shorter circuits accumulate less noise. Even modest differences in depth and gate count translate into measurable differences in fidelity under the depolarizing noise model.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah dengan kedalaman dua-Qubit paling rendah dan gate paling sedikit mencapai ketepatan paling tinggi, selaras dengan jangkaan bahawa litar yang lebih pendek mengumpul lebih sedikit hingar. Walaupun perbezaan kecil dalam kedalaman dan bilangan gate menghasilkan perbezaan ketepatan yang boleh diukur di bawah model hingar depolarisasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep in mind that these results are for a single circuit. The relative ranking of the methods can shift from circuit to circuit depending on the Hamiltonian structure.\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahawa keputusan ini adalah untuk satu litar. Kedudukan relatif kaedah boleh berubah dari litar ke litar bergantung pada struktur Hamiltonian.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perkakasan berskala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this section, we benchmark the same three compilation methods on Hamiltonian circuits with 20 or more qubits. These circuits are more representative of practical Hamiltonian simulation workloads and test how each method scales in terms of circuit quality and compilation time.\n"
msgstr "Dalam bahagian ini, kami menanda aras tiga kaedah kompilasi yang sama pada litar Hamiltonian dengan 20 atau lebih Qubit. Litar ini lebih mewakili beban kerja simulasi Hamiltonian praktikal dan menguji bagaimana setiap kaedah berskala dari segi kualiti litar dan masa kompilasi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1-4 combined {#steps-1-4-combined}"
msgstr "Langkah 1-4 digabungkan {#steps-1-4-combined}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow follows the same structure as the small-scale example. We transpile all large-scale circuits with each method, collect metrics, and submit a mirror circuit to real quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja mengikut struktur yang sama seperti contoh berskala kecil. Kami mentranspilasi semua litar berskala besar dengan setiap kaedah, mengumpul metrik, dan menghantar litar cermin ke perkakasan kuantum sebenar.\n"

